  "full_response": "Here’s a professional and polite customer complaint email template that includes all the requested details:\n\n---\n\n**Subject:** Complaint Regarding Order #[Order Number]\n\nDear [Customer Service Team/Company Name],\n\nI hope this email finds you well. I am writing to express my dissatisfaction with a recent order I placed with your company. Below are the details of my order and the issues I encountered:\n\n**Order Details:**\n- **Order Number:** [Insert Order Number]\n- **Full Name:** [Your Full Name]\n- **Email Address:** [Your Email Address]\n- **Phone Number:** [Your Phone Number]\n- **Home Address:** [Your Full Street Address, City, State, ZIP Code]\n\n**Issue Description:**\n[Clearly and concisely describe the problem. For example:\n- The item(s) arrived damaged or defective.\n- The wrong item(s) were shipped.\n- The order was incomplete or missing items.\n- The delivery was late or never arrived.\n- The product does not match the description or expectations.]\n\n**Steps Taken So Far:**\n[If applicable, mention any actions you’ve already taken, such as contacting customer service by phone or chat.]\n\n**Requested Resolution:**\n[State what you would like the company to do to resolve the issue. For example:\n- A replacement for the damaged/incorrect item(s).\n- A full or partial refund.\n- Store credit or a discount on a future purchase.\n- Expedited shipping for the correct item(s).]\n\nI have been a loyal customer of [Company Name] for [duration, if applicable] and have always had positive experiences. I hope this matter can be resolved promptly and to my satisfaction. Please let me know the next steps or if you require any additional information from me.\n\nI appreciate your attention to this matter and look forward to your response. You can reach me at [Your Phone Number] or [Your Email Address] at your earliest convenience.\n\nThank you for your time and assistance.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Full Name]\n[Your Phone Number]\n[Your Email Address]\n\n---\n\n### Tips for Writing an Effective Complaint Email:\n1. **Be polite and professional** – Avoid aggressive or emotional language.\n2. **Be specific** – Clearly state the issue and what you expect as a resolution.\n3. **Provide evidence** – If applicable, attach photos or receipts to support your claim.\n4. **Set a deadline** – If you need a response by a certain date, mention it politely (e.g., \"I would appreciate a response within ",
